why: いがらし, ゆみこ, 1950- and イガラシ, ユミコ, 1950-. A kana name has no kanji boundary to lean
  on, so the heading is the only thing that says where it divides, and the birth year
  is cataloguing apparatus that has to come off both halves before the reading can
  be compared with ours.
